    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What changed\n\nConsolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**identityKey** = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`. A create is rejected **409** only when a new owner's *whole* key equals an existing owner's.\n\n### New files\n- `OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 shared util: `key(telephone, email, householdId)` builds the key (email lower-cased, null/blank segments empty); `householdId(lastName, address)` holds the stable SHA-256 derivation.\n- `RequireUniqueIdentity.java` \u2014 the single duplicate-detection step. Computes the request's key (deriving the would-be `householdId` from last name + address when `sharesHousehold: true`, else absent) and compares it against every existing owner's key.\n- `DuplicateIdentityException.java` + `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 checked escalation \u2192 409 with body `{\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}`.\n- Escalation YAML wiring the handler.\n\n### Modified\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 replaced `requireUniqueTelephone`/`requireUniqueHousehold`/`requireUniqueEmail` with one `requireUniqueIdentity` step.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema (so it's generated on `OwnerDto` and **returned**).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 populates `identityKey` via `OwnerIdentity.key(...)`, so the returned key matches exactly what the collision check compares.\n- `AssignHouseholdId.java` \u2014 now derives the household id via the shared `OwnerIdentity.householdId(...)`, guaranteeing the check and the assignment produce the same value; javadoc updated.\n\n### Removed\nThe three old `RequireUnique*` functions, their `Duplicate*Exception`/handler classes, and their escalation YAMLs.\n\n### Behaviour change (as specified)\nBecause telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with **different telephones** now have different keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
